id: pm-case-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 quick PR and deep tiers
description: "Preserve required checks and release contracts while reducing repeated PR work. Companion: pm-cli-website-dyhg."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-case#13",performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T14:21:47.360Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T19:03:38.673Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T14:21:50.236Z",codex-sol,"Required checks confirmed: test (22), test (26), codeql. CodeQL remains unfiltered. Plan: one quick npm release gate on Node 26, quick build/tests on Node 22, documentation identity/privacy checks on both, exhaustive npm/Bun gates in a deep workflow. Release rollout files remain owned by pm-ops#272."
  "2026-11-15T14:23:21.562Z",codex-sol,"Successful main run 43705527239 job logs: seeded model 71.197 s at 500 operations; packed consumer acceptance 125.835 s. Hosted execution: Node 22 3m09s; Node 26 11m54s. gh run view returned an empty log, so used the job-log endpoint. Only the 500-operation model needs depth reduction; finite capacity fixtures and the 24-case proposal stay unchanged. Docs privacy suites require compiled modules, so their gate includes a prerequisite build. Integer watchdog scaling covers harness timeouts only."
  "2026-11-15T14:28:25.897Z",codex-sol,"Baseline blocker: tracker:health fails extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (host 2026.11.9; pm-github needs 2026.11.14). Tracked separately as pm-case-health-skew; health gates remain strict. Linked schema/tracker contexts also exposed ambient extension discovery in the plain-tracker fixture; give that fixture its own global PM path. Workflow assertion now follows the health call inside release:check. Initial quick coverage passed 110/111 tests before this fixture correction."
  "2026-11-15T14:29:01.654Z",codex-sol,"Correction after inspecting existing release evidence: the host-version skew is from inherited global extensions, not a package dependency or clean-CI defect. Existing pm-case-release notes already identify this environment boundary. pm-case-health-skew now describes isolation follow-up only. No dependency pin changes are needed; verify local health with an isolated global PM path."
  "2026-11-15T14:30:23.955Z",codex-sol,Final focused linked run in tracker context passes all 35 tests (158.901 s); direct workflow suite passes 3/3 (26.364 s). Strict docs health first installs clone-local merge drivers because this package has no prepare hook. Local SDK health passes with isolated global PM settings. Typecheck and lint pass. No product timeout or coverage policy changed.
  "2026-11-15T14:32:01.886Z",codex-sol,"Final direct quick coverage PASSED: 111/111 tests; all statements, branches, functions and lines 100% across the unchanged nine emitted runtime files. No missing late-seed branches. Disposable clone proof: merge install followed by strict pm health passes with zero warnings. Changelog and identity gates pass. PR #13 opened; CI run 43724796981 and CodeQL run 43724796915 are queued. Queue-inclusive required-check wall time is unavailable; not waiting for CI. Full depth and packed/revert acceptance remain for remote tiers."
  "2026-11-15T18:49:57.329Z",codex-sol,"Round C: verify the supplied review findings, repair failing checks, audit CI tier boundaries and harness controls, and run focused gates. Review threads remain untouched; no merge or closure."
  "2026-11-15T18:56:06.387Z",codex-sol,"Failed run 43724887689 reached changelog checking: the in-progress CI task was missing from generated content. Regenerate with the package script. Self-review checks documentation/privacy/identity gates, unscaled product budgets, integer timeouts, validation before spawn, platform filenames and generated-only quick thresholds."
  "2026-11-15T18:57:51.525Z",codex-sol,"Self-review additionally restores input-sensitive docs-path gates: identity/privacy, packaging and attestation validation, plus applicable docs/tooling tests. These cheap-path requirements are in the rollout template. New failure-injection tests execute each documentation block."
  "2026-11-15T19:03:37.913Z",codex-sol,"Round C validation passed: typecheck, test TypeScript compilation, focused behavior and workflow/tooling suites, strict unique-key YAML parsing, and package changelog regeneration/check. Lint passed where the package provides a lint script; packages without one passed their existing docstring gate. No configured coverage source changed, so no package coverage run was added. Existing isolated coverage-tooling fixtures are part of the focused tooling suites. All supplied review findings are valid and repaired. Self-review additionally preserves executable tracker scans and all applicable docs/privacy/identity/package/attestation gates. Product budgets and coverage thresholds remain unchanged. Validation uses the local Node 24 runtime; Node 22/26, native Windows and deep runtime certification remain CI evidence. Threads untouched; no merge or item closure. Release ownership after recording this evidence."
